
# Amortization Calculator

A command-line financial interest and amortization calculator built entirely in Python without external dependencies. This project serves as a hands-on exercise for mastering AI-assisted development workflows, iterative prompt engineering, and code debugging.

## Features
* **Pure Python Implementation:** Relies solely on native Python libraries for clean portability.
* **Robust Input Validation:** Catches non-numeric entries, negative values, and zero-term edge cases.
* **Zero-Interest Handling:** Gracefully handles 0% interest rate loans without causing division-by-zero errors.
* **Precision Rounding & Drift Protection:** Automatically corrects for floating-point rounding drift on the final payment cycle.

## Requirements
* Python 3.8 or higher.

## Usage
1. Clone the repository:
   ```bash
   git clone [https://github.com/your-username/amortization-calculator.git](https://github.com/your-username/amortization-calculator.git)
   cd amortization-calculator
